WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.791 --> 00:00:32.083
After explaining that He is the source

2
00:00:32.083 --> 00:00:34.208
of all qualities in all worlds,

3
00:00:34.208 --> 00:00:36.875
now in the sixth verse of the tenth chapter,

4
00:00:36.875 --> 00:00:40.708
Lord Krishna explains that all the great rishis,

5
00:00:40.708 --> 00:00:44.666
Manu – the original ancestor
of humanity – and ultimately

6
00:00:44.666 --> 00:00:48.208
all living beings have been born from Him.

7
00:00:53.125 --> 00:00:54.416
In this verse, Lord Krishna

8
00:00:54.416 --> 00:00:58.791
presents Himself as the supreme creator.

9
00:00:58.791 --> 00:01:01.375
He says that He is not only

10
00:01:01.375 --> 00:01:03.250
of the material world,

11
00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:06.625
but also of the rishis and Manus the source.

12
00:01:06.625 --> 00:01:10.791
Manu, who is the original
ancestor of human society,

13
00:01:10.791 --> 00:01:14.875
the Sapta Rishis, the four Kumaras,
and the fourteen Manus,

14
00:01:14.875 --> 00:01:17.500
all of them were born from Brahma,

15
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.833
and Brahma himself

16
00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:21.958
was born from Lord Krishna,

17
00:01:21.958 --> 00:01:24.833
from His Brahman form manifested.

18
00:01:24.833 --> 00:01:27.291
This shows Lord Krishna's extraordinary

19
00:01:27.291 --> 00:01:29.708
power of creation.

20
00:01:29.708 --> 00:01:31.791
Bhrigu, Marichi,

21
00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:36.208
Atri, Pulastya, Pulaha, Kratu, and Vasishtha –

22
00:01:36.208 --> 00:01:37.750
these seven great rishis

23
00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:38.541
for their knowledge

24
00:01:38.541 --> 00:01:41.000
and guidance to humanity

25
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.375
are honoured in this world.

26
00:01:43.375 --> 00:01:47.750
Before them, the four Kumaras –
Sanaka, Sanandana, Sanatana,

27
00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.041
and Sanat-Kumar –

28
00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:50.208
from Brahma's

29
00:01:50.208 --> 00:01:52.250
desire to create were born,

30
00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:56.125
who are symbols of pure
knowledge and detachment.

31
00:01:56.125 --> 00:01:59.250
Beginning with Svayambhuva Manu,

32
00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.833
the fourteen Manus in different ages

33
00:02:01.833 --> 00:02:03.416
for governing the world

34
00:02:03.416 --> 00:02:07.500
and of civilisation for maintaining
continuity are responsible.

35
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.041
Lord Krishna's statement

36
00:02:09.041 --> 00:02:09.958
that all beings

37
00:02:09.958 --> 00:02:12.791
from these ancestral figures are born

38
00:02:12.791 --> 00:02:16.125
reminds us of our divine source.

39
00:02:16.125 --> 00:02:19.333
Through the Manus and rishis, the line of descent

40
00:02:19.333 --> 00:02:22.166
connects us back to Lord Krishna.

41
00:02:22.166 --> 00:02:24.500
This is not just physical form,

42
00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:27.958
but also of these great
souls the qualities, actions,

43
00:02:27.958 --> 00:02:31.958
and knowledge – Lord Krishna
alone is the source.

44
00:02:31.958 --> 00:02:35.583
This verse also subtly tells that although

45
00:02:35.583 --> 00:02:39.958
these great ancestors are deeply revered, but

46
00:02:39.958 --> 00:02:42.666
they too are under Lord Krishna.

47
00:02:42.666 --> 00:02:44.875
Even the greatest rishis and devas

48
00:02:44.875 --> 00:02:47.875
without His grace His divine form

49
00:02:47.875 --> 00:02:50.458
cannot fully understand.

50
00:02:50.458 --> 00:02:52.375
Knowing that all of creation

51
00:02:52.375 --> 00:02:55.500
flows from Lord Krishna, a person

52
00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:58.208
develops humility and devotion,

53
00:02:58.208 --> 00:03:00.833
understanding that our ultimate identity

54
00:03:00.833 --> 00:03:04.916
and life's purpose lie within Him.

55
00:03:04.916 --> 00:03:07.208
Through this knowledge, Lord Krishna

56
00:03:07.208 --> 00:03:08.875
asks us, instead of on our lineage

57
00:03:08.875 --> 00:03:11.750
or achievements taking pride,

58
00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:14.666
to take pride in that bond

59
00:03:14.666 --> 00:03:18.000
which is between us and Lord Krishna.

60
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.083
By this alone, to achieve life's goal

61
00:03:21.083 --> 00:03:22.916
He inspires us.

62
00:03:27.375 --> 00:03:30.833
Have you ever thought

63
00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:32.750
on what basis

64
00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:39.375
do people judge each other?

65
00:03:39.375 --> 00:03:41.166
In life,

66
00:03:41.166 --> 00:03:44.458
to judge people by their outer form,

67
00:03:44.458 --> 00:03:47.625
their appearance, their lineage, or

68
00:03:47.625 --> 00:03:52.250
their wealth – on these bases it is easy.

69
00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:55.291
But remember,

70
00:03:55.291 --> 00:03:59.833
I am the original source of all.

71
00:03:59.833 --> 00:04:04.375
Every being, whatever their background

72
00:04:04.375 --> 00:04:08.000
or circumstance may be,

73
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.708
ultimately

74
00:04:09.708 --> 00:04:14.708
has come from Me.

75
00:04:14.708 --> 00:04:16.208
When you

76
00:04:16.208 --> 00:04:20.291
focus your attention, on this truth

77
00:04:20.291 --> 00:04:23.291
then to see everyone with equal respect

78
00:04:23.291 --> 00:04:27.500
and compassion becomes natural.

79
00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:31.041
To judge this on the basis of outer appearance

80
00:04:31.041 --> 00:04:33.916
is just like

81
00:04:33.916 --> 00:04:37.500
by looking only at the tree's leaves

82
00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:41.833
judging its strength

83
00:04:41.833 --> 00:04:45.125
and forgetting its roots.

84
00:04:45.125 --> 00:04:48.833
At the root of everyone's existence

85
00:04:48.833 --> 00:04:51.833
I alone am there.

86
00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:54.500
By remembering this,

87
00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.375
how you see others

88
00:04:57.375 --> 00:05:00.625
your perspective changes.

89
00:05:00.625 --> 00:05:02.875
Instead of differences,

90
00:05:02.875 --> 00:05:07.958
you begin to see that deep bond

91
00:05:07.958 --> 00:05:10.958
which all living beings

92
00:05:10.958 --> 00:05:13.333
binds in unity.

93
00:05:13.333 --> 00:05:17.625
Practise this mindset every day.

94
00:05:17.625 --> 00:05:18.750
Before forming

95
00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.625
any opinion, pause, take a breath,

96
00:05:22.625 --> 00:05:24.833
and remember the divine

97
00:05:24.833 --> 00:05:28.250
spark within everyone.

98
00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:29.666
When you

99
00:05:29.666 --> 00:05:33.583
overcome the tendency to judge,

100
00:05:33.583 --> 00:05:37.333
and focus on the deeper connection,

101
00:05:37.333 --> 00:05:39.125
then your conduct

102
00:05:39.125 --> 00:05:43.375
naturally becomes more loving

103
00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:46.500
and inclusive.

104
00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:49.083
When you see all connected by

105
00:05:49.083 --> 00:05:52.416
one divine thread,

106
00:05:52.416 --> 00:05:57.500
then you too will connect
with that supreme truth

107
00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:00.208
which since eternity

108
00:06:00.208 --> 00:06:03.000
has been the foundation of all.

109
00:06:07.583 --> 00:06:10.916
You may have seen

110
00:06:10.916 --> 00:06:12.958
in society

111
00:06:12.958 --> 00:06:15.958
how the pride of lineage

112
00:06:15.958 --> 00:06:20.750
creates distance in relationships.

113
00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:25.583
In families, pride in one's lineage often

114
00:06:25.583 --> 00:06:31.500
shapes identity and one's own values.

115
00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:34.291
While appreciating one's heritage

116
00:06:34.291 --> 00:06:36.500
is natural,

117
00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:40.875
it is essential to remember this –

118
00:06:40.875 --> 00:06:44.250
ultimately, every soul

119
00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.875
to its original source

120
00:06:47.875 --> 00:06:49.916
is connected to Me.

121
00:06:49.916 --> 00:06:52.250
The great rishis, the Manus,

122
00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:56.333
and all living beings' origin

123
00:06:56.333 --> 00:06:58.666
is in Me,

124
00:06:58.666 --> 00:07:01.625
which makes every soul

125
00:07:01.625 --> 00:07:05.875
part of a divine lineage.

126
00:07:05.875 --> 00:07:08.208
Just as buttermilk,

127
00:07:08.208 --> 00:07:12.041
curd, ghee, butter, paneer, khoya

128
00:07:12.041 --> 00:07:14.500
look different in form,

129
00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.291
but

130
00:07:16.291 --> 00:07:19.000
the root of all is

131
00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.083
milk.

132
00:07:21.083 --> 00:07:24.958
In the same way, existence has many forms,

133
00:07:24.958 --> 00:07:29.333
but the root of all

134
00:07:29.333 --> 00:07:31.041
is Me.

135
00:07:31.041 --> 00:07:35.666
When this understanding is absorbed deeply,

136
00:07:35.666 --> 00:07:39.166
then the barriers of caste, status, or family pride

137
00:07:39.166 --> 00:07:43.625
that often

138
00:07:43.625 --> 00:07:47.125
give birth to discrimination dissolve.

139
00:07:47.125 --> 00:07:48.791
See,

140
00:07:48.791 --> 00:07:52.875
in a family a father tells his son –

141
00:07:52.875 --> 00:07:56.541
'We are of such-and-such caste,

142
00:07:56.541 --> 00:07:59.750
that is why we are superior.'

143
00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:05.208
How does this plant arrogance in his mind?

144
00:08:05.208 --> 00:08:08.666
Imagine a society of such a world,

145
00:08:08.666 --> 00:08:10.416
a society

146
00:08:10.416 --> 00:08:16.000
where every family teaches
its children this truth –

147
00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.666
that in all

148
00:08:17.666 --> 00:08:20.333
fundamentally the same

149
00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:23.958
divinity lives.

150
00:08:23.958 --> 00:08:25.375
Will this not among people

151
00:08:25.375 --> 00:08:29.125
awaken more respect and harmony?

152
00:08:29.125 --> 00:08:31.333
As a family,

153
00:08:31.333 --> 00:08:34.458
understand this knowledge deeply.

154
00:08:34.458 --> 00:08:38.000
With every person, beyond their background,

155
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:43.791
practise treating them with respect.

156
00:08:43.791 --> 00:08:46.291
Teach your young ones

157
00:08:46.291 --> 00:08:47.708
that true greatness

158
00:08:47.708 --> 00:08:48.833
is not in being born

159
00:08:48.833 --> 00:08:51.791
into our particular family,

160
00:08:51.791 --> 00:08:55.541
but in living life with humility

161
00:08:55.541 --> 00:08:57.750
and for others contributing –

162
00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:59.666
in that it lies.

163
00:08:59.666 --> 00:09:02.458
Are you teaching your family

164
00:09:02.458 --> 00:09:07.583
about this divine bond?

165
00:09:07.583 --> 00:09:11.333
When families are based on this truth,

166
00:09:11.333 --> 00:09:14.708
only then will true unity in society

167
00:09:14.708 --> 00:09:17.916
and mutual respect come.

168
00:09:22.416 --> 00:09:24.791
In your office,

169
00:09:24.791 --> 00:09:27.833
do people based on their position

170
00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:32.041
receive different levels of respect?

171
00:09:32.041 --> 00:09:33.875
At the workplace,

172
00:09:33.875 --> 00:09:36.833
evaluating people based on their positions,

173
00:09:36.833 --> 00:09:40.916
salary, or outward achievements

174
00:09:40.916 --> 00:09:43.791
seems easy.

175
00:09:43.791 --> 00:09:44.958
But

176
00:09:44.958 --> 00:09:48.250
when you look beyond these identities,

177
00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:51.541
and experience that all

178
00:09:51.541 --> 00:09:55.708
from the same supreme source – that is,

179
00:09:55.708 --> 00:09:58.166
from Me –

180
00:09:58.166 --> 00:10:00.291
then mutual respect and

181
00:10:00.291 --> 00:10:03.833
a culture of understanding you nurture.

182
00:10:03.833 --> 00:10:04.791
As a leader

183
00:10:04.791 --> 00:10:06.666
or team member,

184
00:10:06.666 --> 00:10:09.041
to evaluate someone only

185
00:10:09.041 --> 00:10:12.708
on the basis of their position or appearance

186
00:10:12.708 --> 00:10:15.958
your ability to build real connections

187
00:10:15.958 --> 00:10:19.916
with them limits.

188
00:10:19.916 --> 00:10:21.583
Think –

189
00:10:21.583 --> 00:10:24.333
if at the office a cleaning staff member

190
00:10:24.333 --> 00:10:29.875
is considered less important than a manager,

191
00:10:29.875 --> 00:10:32.375
is this perspective correct?

192
00:10:32.375 --> 00:10:35.125
Remember, every person

193
00:10:35.125 --> 00:10:38.000
brings different unique qualities.

194
00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.500
These qualities

195
00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:43.166
come from that same all-pervading energy

196
00:10:43.166 --> 00:10:45.875
which flows through all beings.

197
00:10:45.875 --> 00:10:49.375
Just as all the organs of the body

198
00:10:49.375 --> 00:10:51.500
perform different functions

199
00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:56.000
and their harmony is what
creates a healthy body,

200
00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.333
in the same way

201
00:10:57.333 --> 00:11:02.375
every employee has their
own unique contribution.

202
00:11:02.375 --> 00:11:04.750
When you understand this,

203
00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:07.166
then you build trustworthy

204
00:11:07.166 --> 00:11:11.041
and uniting relationships.

205
00:11:11.041 --> 00:11:15.458
By treating all with equal respect

206
00:11:15.458 --> 00:11:19.166
and by acknowledging that deep bond

207
00:11:19.166 --> 00:11:23.625
which unites all beings,

208
00:11:23.625 --> 00:11:26.916
you create a more harmonious

209
00:11:26.916 --> 00:11:30.500
and cooperative environment.

210
00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:35.333
Workplaces flourish when every person

211
00:11:35.333 --> 00:11:39.083
feels themselves valued,

212
00:11:39.083 --> 00:11:42.541
not for their outer form,

213
00:11:42.541 --> 00:11:47.500
but for their meaningful contribution.

214
00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:49.916
When at the workplace all

215
00:11:49.916 --> 00:11:55.125
are given equal respect,
only then will true success

216
00:11:55.125 --> 00:11:56.166
and everyone

217
00:11:56.166 --> 00:12:00.250
in their work will find satisfaction.

218
00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:03.291
With this perspective, true success

219
00:12:03.291 --> 00:12:08.375
and satisfaction in everyone's
work will be found.
